package views

templ sustainability() {
    <h2 id="sustainability" class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold p-4 text-center md:text-left section-scroll">Sustainability</h2>
    @whatSustainable()
    @virtualLCA()
    @whySustainable()
    }

templ whatSustainable() {
    <section class="p-4" aria-label="what is sustainable development?">
        <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl pb-4 text-center md:text-left">What is Sustainable Software Development?</h3>
        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl pb-4">
        Sustainable Development is development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future
        generations to meet their own needs. In Software Engineering terms, Sustainable Development is a systems thinking
        approach to development that focuses on how an application and its parts affect the environment over time.
        </p>

        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl">
        We design all our applications with these principles in mind and hope to inspire our collaborators / stakeholders to
        consider the virtual life cycle assessment when designing software.
        </p>
    </section>
    }

templ virtualLCA() {
    <section class="p-4 pt-8" aria-label="life cycle assessment of software">
        <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl pb-4 text-center md:text-left">What is the Life Cycle Assessment of a software product?</h3>

        // defining LCA
        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl pb-4">
        A Life Cycle Assessment (LCA), is the methodology for assessing the environmental impact associated with all the stages
        of a commercial product, process, or service. This takes into account the materials used to produce it, manufacturing,
           packaging, distribution, usage, & disposal.
        </p>

        // applying LCAs to digital products
        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl">
            With a digital product like a web application for example, it primarily uses energy in three key parts of its life
            cycle:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-base md:text-2xl pl-6 pb-4" style="list-style-type: circle; line-height: 180%;">
            <li>The creation, testing, launch, and maintenance of applications.</li>

            <li>The hosting and serving of applications.</li>

            <li>The download and interaction of users with applications.</li>
        </ul>

        // virtual LCAs
        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl">
            Therefore a Virtual LCA would look something like this:
        </p>

        <ul class="text-base md:text-2xl pl-6" style="list-style-type: circle; line-height: 180%;">
            <li>Materials: Software and visual assets</li>

            <li>Manufacturing: Design and development</li>

            <li>Packaging: Uploaded to the internet</li>

            <li>Distribution: Downloaded through network</li>

            <li>Usage: Interaction, UX, completing tasks</li>

            <li>Disposal: Data erased from client</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    }

templ whySustainable() {
    <section class="p-4 pt-8" aria-label="why sustainable development is important">
        <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl pb-4 text-center md:text-left">Why Sustainable Software Development is important for stakeholders and our planet</h3>
        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl pb-4">
        Did you know if the internet was a country it would be the 5th largest producer of GHG in the world? It turns out that
        the digital medium isn’t as green as we think it is. The data centers that power the applications we enjoy produce tons
        of emissions.
        </p>

        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl pb-4">
        It’s important that we power our web applications with clean renewable energy and reduce energy use by building
        efficient software. Doing this is not only good for our planet, it’s good for your users and your bottom line.
        </p>

        <p class="text-base md:text-2xl">
        When sustainable development principles are embraced you:
        </p>

        <ul class="text-base md:text-2xl pl-6" style="list-style-type: circle; line-height: 180%;">
            <li>Improve performance: via lean, fast loading pages</li>

            <li>Improve usability: Clear navigation and messaging</li>

            <li>Improve Search engine results: Easily crawled websites that drive traffic and deliver answers quickly</li>

            <li>Improve accessibility: Relevant content delivered quickly across platforms and devices</li>

            <li>Decreased environmental impact: Solutions powered by renewable energy</li>

            <li>Cost Savings: Via efficient applications that send less data to users</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    }
